.TH BOSWAS-CONTROL-CENTER 1 "October 2026" "boswas-control-center 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-control-center \- settings hub of Boswas OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-control-center
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR page ]
.br
.B boswas-control-center
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-control-center
is Boswas Control Center, the settings hub of Boswas OS. It has one page per
area. Each page explains the state of the device and opens the matching KDE
settings module with
.BR kcmshell6 (1)
for everything that is configured there.
.PP
The pages are Personalization (Boswas desktop presets and the KDE
appearance modules), Network, Bluetooth, Display, Sound, Power, Storage,
Applications (the Boswas Software Center), Windows Compatibility, Security
(the Boswas Security Center), Users, Updates (the Boswas Update Center),
Devices, Privacy, System and About Boswas OS. In a live session an Install
Boswas OS page explains how to restart into the installer.
.PP
The Security Center shows the local posture checks of
.B boswas \-\-json status
and the state of the Boswas device agent. Each item is shown as Secure,
Warning, Attention, Info, Not available or Error, always as text and as an
icon. The checks are a local self\-assessment of the device, not remote
attestation.
.PP
The Update Center shows whether automatic security updates are enabled, read
from the APT periodic settings, and when they last ran. It changes nothing:
updates are installed automatically, and this release has no manual updater.
.PP
The Software Center lists the installed applications in three groups: Boswas
applications, Windows applications (from the user's Boswas session service)
and the other desktop applications. It opens native applications with
.BR kstart (1).
Windows applications are managed in the Compatibility Manager and are never
started by Control Center. Installing new software is not possible here.
.PP
Control Center runs as the desktop user and never as root. It starts only the
programs it knows (boswas, boswas\-preset, kcmshell6, kstart, kioclient,
dolphin, partitionmanager, kinfocenter, boswas\-compat\-manager, plasmashell,
apt\-config and, in a live session after confirmation, systemctl reboot), each
with a fixed argument list and a timeout, and never through a shell.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " page"
Open the window at
.IR page :
one of personalization, network, bluetooth, display, sound, power, storage,
applications, windows, security, users, updates, devices, privacy, system,
about or install. The install page exists only in a live session.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Up, Down
In the category list: switch pages.
.TP
.B F5
Refresh the current page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Search the installed applications.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/boswas\-agent/agent.sock
The Boswas device agent, used read\-only for the device, policy, privacy and
runtime status.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/boswas/session.sock
The user's Boswas session service, used read\-only for the Windows
applications and the compatibility runtime.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/boswas/release
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/boswas/image\-info
The Boswas OS version and build shown on the About page.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window was closed normally; 4 when started as root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas (1),
.BR boswas\-compat\-manager (1),
.BR kcmshell6 (1)
